.TH DOME-XR 1 "2026-10-20" "de-xr" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dome\-xr \- present the DomeD desktop in OpenXR
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
dome\-xr [\-\-server URL] [\-\-frames N] [\-\-capture DIR]
        [\-\-report FILE] [\-\-standalone] [\-\-placement N]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Connect to the local DomeD bridge and submit live Wayland client textures and shell surfaces to OpenXR. The default mode requests an overlay or transparent blend mode when supported.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B "\-\-server URL"
DomeD bridge URL, normally http://127.0.0.1:49640.
.TP
.B "\-\-standalone"
Request a primary XR session rather than the default overlay.
.TP
.B "\-\-placement N"
Select the runtime overlay placement.
.TP
.B "\-\-frames N"
Exit after N frames for a bounded diagnostic run.
.TP
.B "\-\-capture DIR"
Save diagnostic client texture captures to DIR; these are not headset eye captures.
.TP
.B "\-\-report FILE"
Write a diagnostic report.
.TP
.B "\-\-help"
Show usage.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
XR_RUNTIME_JSON selects the OpenXR runtime manifest. Use a runtime that supports the required composition layers.
.SH SEE ALSO
dome\-compositor(1), dome\-preview(1)
